sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant RC as RunCommand
    participant Sub as OS Subprocess
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant SSM as AWS SSM
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant DB as MongoDB

    User->>RC: baas run <type> [params] [--instance-type] [--timeout] [--skip-build] [--ami-id]
    Note over RC: validate type in {jmh, jmh-with-async, jmh-with-prof, jcstress}<br/>ConfigService.load() from ~/.baas/config.yaml
    RC->>Sub: git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD
    Sub-->>RC: current branch name
    RC->>SSM: ssm.getParameter(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id)
    SSM-->>RC: amiId, or ParameterNotFound
    RC->>EC2: ec2.describeImages(amiId)
    EC2-->>RC: image + tags (baas-image-version), or InvalidAMIID.NotFound
    Note over RC: no image -> exit 1 naming `baas admin build-image`.<br/>Deliberately FIRST: before the Maven build and before any<br/>upload, so a missing image costs two API calls.<br/>There is no fallback to AL2023 + yum.
    opt --skip-build = false (default)
        RC->>Sub: mvn clean package -q -DskipTests
        Sub-->>RC: BUILD SUCCESS or RuntimeException on failure
    end
    Note over RC: generate requestId = type-yyyyMMdd_HHmmss<br/>resultPath = branch/type/yyyyMMdd_HHmmss
    RC->>S3: s3.putObject(bucket, runs/requestId/benchmark.jar)
    S3-->>RC: PutObjectResponse
    Note over RC: UserDataScriptBuilder.build() -- installs NOTHING;<br/>the toolchain is baked into the AMI.<br/>Script captures environment.json + packages.txt and uploads<br/>them BEFORE the benchmark, so a crash still leaves a record,<br/>downloads benchmark-runner.jar from S3 or GitHub Releases,<br/>fetches MONGO_CONNECTION_STRING from SSM,<br/>runs: timeout N java -jar benchmark-runner.jar type<br/>--tag imageVersion=... --tag instanceType=... ...<br/>writes run-status sentinel to S3<br/>self-terminates the EC2 instance
    RC->>EC2: ec2.runInstances(amiId, instanceType, subnetId, sgId, instanceProfile, userData, tags)
    Note over EC2: min=1 max=1<br/>shutdownBehavior=TERMINATE<br/>IMDSv2 required<br/>tags: baas-role=benchmark-runner
    EC2-->>RC: instanceId
    Note over RC: register JVM shutdown hook<br/>ec2.terminateInstances(instanceId) on Ctrl+C
    loop poll every 15 seconds
        RC->>S3: s3.getObjectAsBytes(resultPath/run-status)
        S3-->>RC: completed or failed:N or absent -- sleep 15s and retry
    end
    RC->>SSM: ssm.getParameter(/<prefix>/mongo/connection-string, withDecryption=true)
    SSM-->>RC: mongoUri
    RC->>DB: find({_id.requestId: requestId}) on jmh_benchmarks
    DB-->>RC: BENCHMARK | MODE | SCORE | ERROR | UNIT
    RC-->>User: print results table and exit 0
